## Context

pep-erg-v1.md predates three design decisions that are now implemented but
never written up as rationale:

1. **Tags header.** The PEP defines exactly 5 headers; Tags was added later.
   The PEP should document the design decision: why Tags, why this closed set
   of values, why repeatable.

2. **Closed-path criterion.** The PEP describes the Closed: header mechanism but
   omits the path-based closed test (directory named `closed/`, filename containing
   `-closed`, etc.). Add the rationale: why two mechanisms, when each is appropriate.

3. **`archive/` → `closed/` promotion.** The PEP mentions both `archive/` and `closed/`
   as valid layouts. The decision to canonicalise `closed/` and migrate `archive/`
   automatically was made later. Document this as a deliberate simplification.

## Actions
1. Add a "Tags" section to pep-erg-v1.md with rationale.
2. Extend the closed-status section to cover path-based detection and its rationale.
3. Add a note on the archive→closed canonicalisation decision.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] PEP documents Tags header with rationale
- [ ] PEP documents closed-path criterion alongside header criterion
- [ ] PEP explains archive→closed canonicalisation
